<p>The Seoul High Court on Tuesday increased former South Korean first lady Kim Keon Hee’s corruption sentence to four years in prison from 20 months after convicting her of stock price manipulation and bribery. Kim is the wife of ousted former President Yoon Suk Yeol. The court reversed a lower-court acquittal on market-related charges, finding that Kim took part in manipulating the share price of Deutsch Motors and a thinly traded Korean stock through coordinated trades. It also found that she accepted luxury gifts, including Chanel bags and a Graff necklace, from figures linked to the Unification Church, whose representatives expected political favors. Kim has denied the charges and has been jailed since August.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vs02utoiKG5yqChJvlwHkpDobWyehwZvSA7I-Rrb72FAi0Adt2bSiTxEMnNh08keuiQoVZELGV7-4_fP_DWZ48A97XuiU5w2c38LqLfzIHpj_UX1jR2Vyz1EX3U6bep8HqYxKzPyZD_OF76EiJ_jgliZV0MwkGtsjHQWBeoH2Qfibjt47_J_U6IfWLiV8H3LCdebFpP2mBOEp1NngLm6eoSCpMx55lMi8uruW3ehJnTRfY1IhIV-04Vn0xIj_VdrBRY22Qnndtjw8X24iWRb8-bw_K5XSPWu8-vSvLpMAoFMDsO9bKPNbqo1ktz2NO8GU3WbEP8a4uNsVL3JhUQNPEr3zUdplRVsTJxy443-tu1_sDyNHRmqeuH0dmQtVyXbMxWKoI3kgmocg5OWXZtRJ8msADlDVeTIgtvx_ykFCfQVc55Zkrp7HvZOdYc' alt='Former South Korean first lady Kim Keon Hee connected to the Seoul High Court corruption ruling.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Trading role: The appellate court said Kim provided large sums and securities accounts used by market-manipulation actors, including a 2 billion won account provided to Black Pearl Invest in October 2010.</li><li>Sentence terms: The court also imposed a 50 million won fine, ordered the confiscation of a Graff necklace valued at 62.2 million won, and ordered 20.94 million won in additional collection.</li><li>Acquitted count: The appellate panel upheld Kim’s acquittal on allegations that she received free polling results from political broker Myung Tae-kyun and intervened in People Power Party nominations.</li><li>Lower-court error: The appellate court said the statute of limitations had not expired on the Deutsch Motors allegation and faulted the trial court’s ruling for misapplying legal principles.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Seoul High Court: The panel said Kim used her status as the president’s spouse in influence-peddling conduct and had not acknowledged her responsibility. (<a href='https://www.donga.com/news/Politics/article/all/20260429/133831314/2'>Dong-A Ilbo</a>)</li><li>Kim Keon Hee&#x27;s defense team: Her lawyers said they would take the case to the Supreme Court. (<a href='https://news.pts.org.tw/article/805866'>PTS</a>)</li><li>Special counsel prosecutors: The special counsel team asked the appeals court to impose a 15-year sentence. (<a href='https://www.mbn.co.kr/pages/news/newsView.php?category=mbn00009&amp;news_seq_no=5190801'>MBN</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3351685/south-korean-court-increases-kim-keon-hees-corruption-sentence-4-years'>South Korean court increases Kim Keon-hee’s corruption sentence to 4 years</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/28/g-s1-119050/south-korean-court-extends-prison-sentence-for-wife-of-ousted-president'>South Korean court extends prison sentence for wife of ousted president</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-ex-first-lady-kim-handed-longer-graft-sentence/a-76964144'>South Korea: Ex-first lady Kim handed longer graft sentence</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/south-korean-court-convicts-wife-ousted-president-yoon-132446125'>South Korean court convicts of wife of ousted President Yoon on corruption charges</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260428-south-korean-court-increases-ex-first-lady-s-graft-sentence'>The Seoul High Court sentences former South Korean first lady Kim Keon Hee to four years in prison after convicting her of stock price manipulat